  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We have $-3\\in [a]_{8}$ if \n\n$$\n-3≡a\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $-3\\in [13]_{8}$ because $-3≡13\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$ $\\,✓$\n\n- $-3\\notin [17]_{8}$ because $-3≢17\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $-3\\in [-11]_{8}$ because $-3≡-11\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
